## Case: legacy-99-idiom2-m07-ext-method
id: "legacy.99_idiom2.m07_ext_method"
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "ext_method.at"
```auto
// Plan 514 W1-2 探针 m07：ext 扩展方法（读字段 + ext 内字段写）
type Num {
    v int
    fn get() int { return .v }
    static fn new(v int) Num { return Num(v) }
}
ext Num {
    fn double() int { return .v * 2 }
    fn bump() {
        .v = .v + 1
    }
}
fn main() {
    let n = Num.new(21)
    print(f"get=${n.get()}")
    print(f"double=${n.double()}")
    var m = Num.new(5)
    m.bump()
    print(f"bumped=${m.get()}")
}
```

### VM result
#ignore
check-id: "vm-stdout"

```text
get=21
double=42
bumped=6
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
channel: "unit"

#### stdout

```text
get=21
double=42
bumped=6
```

## Case: legacy-24-generics-001-list-struct
id: "legacy.24_generics.001_list_struct"
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "list_struct.at"
```auto
type Note { id int; title str }

fn main() {
    let notes = List<Note>.new([
        Note { id: 0, title: "first" },
        Note { id: 1, title: "second" },
    ])
    var count = 0
    for n in notes {
        count = count + 1
    }
    print(count)
}
```

